     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg per day. That is twice the usual maximum of about 2,550 mg per day (immediate-release, labeled maximum). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 850 mg to 1,000 mg per dose. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nPossible intended orders include:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg per day and the maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg per day.\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 1,500 mg per day.\n- **1,700 mg per day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily. This could be what was meant if \"1700\" was the daily total.\n\nPlease confirm the dose you intended, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, let me know the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was confirmed."
      }
     ],
